# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and sends these headers with every response.
#
# X-Robots-Tag does the same job as the noindex meta tag in template.html, but
# at the HTTP level, so it also covers anything that is not HTML.
#
# Deliberately NOT using "Disallow: /" in robots.txt: that blocks crawling, and
# a crawler that never fetches the page never sees the noindex instruction, so
# the URL can still show up in results as a bare link. Letting crawlers in and
# telling them not to index is the combination that actually de-indexes.
#
# Remove this file, robots.txt and the meta tags together if this ever becomes
# a publication rather than a reading tool.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
